---
/** The Kit. Every fact on this page comes from the CAD notes (~/workspace/SLDP CAD on the build
    machine) or from the team poster (docs/README.md, Theme). Do not add a spec, a count or a
    price that is not in one of those. The models are exported by scripts/step_to_glb.py:
    when the CAD version changes, re-export and change the captions and the Status row.
    Since 2026-11-23 the page shows Final v3, and its numbers are from the READMEs of
    Final v1 and Final v3 in the CAD folder. The prices under "What it costs" are the team's
    cost table of 2026-11-24 (docs/cost-table-2026-11-24.png), kept in src/data/compare.ts. */
import Base from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import ModelViewer from '../components/ModelViewer.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../components/SectionLabel.astro';
import ProcessRail from '../components/ProcessRail.astro';
import CircuitDiagram from '../components/CircuitDiagram.astro';
import { p, KIT_REQUEST } from '../lib/url';
import { PORTIONS } from '../lib/lessons';
import { cost, costTotals, money } from '../data/compare';
import { printed, bought, needs, CLASS_SIZE, GROUP } from '../data/kit';

const specs = [
  { k: 'Controller', v: 'Arduino Mega 2560' },
  { k: 'Fingers', v: 'Four finger modules and a thumb' },
  { k: 'Motors', v: 'Six DC motors: one in each finger, two in the thumb' },
  { k: 'Finger drive', v: 'The motor turns a threaded rod, which pulls the finger closed' },
  { k: 'Finger curl', v: 'Straight to 72°' },
  { k: 'Finger module', v: '33 mm wide, 291 mm long (about 1.3 × 11.5 in)' },
  { k: 'Printed parts', v: 'PLA plastic on an ordinary 3D printer, with no support material' },
  { k: 'Size', v: 'About 32 × 26 × 11 cm (12.6 × 10.2 × 4.3 in), lying flat with the thumb out to the side' },
  { k: 'Ages', v: '11 and up' },
];

const bill = costTotals();
const classHands = CLASS_SIZE / GROUP;
const portionSteps = PORTIONS.map((pt) => ({ title: pt.label, body: pt.blurb }));
---
<Base title="The Kit" description="The HelpingHand kit: a modular robotic hand that students design, wire, and program themselves.">
  <PageHeader
    title="A robotic hand students build themselves."
    lede="HelpingHand is a modular robotic hand that students design, wire, and program themselves. They learn mechanics, circuits, and coding one lesson at a time, not by following a manual."
  >
    {/* The page's one status line. The captions and the tables below say nothing more about it. */}
    <p class="meta mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
      <span class="badge badge-demo">Prototype</span>
      <span>This is the team's current design. The first full hand is not printed yet.</span>
    </p>
  </PageHeader>

  <section class="section">
    <SectionLabel>The hand</SectionLabel>
    <div class="mt-8 grid items-start gap-x-12 gap-y-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.25fr)_minmax(0,1fr)]">
      <ModelViewer
        src="/models/hand-final-v3.glb"
        alt="3D model of the HelpingHand: four fingers and a thumb on a palm, with the electronics under a curved shell on the back"
        label="The whole hand"
        height="h-[22rem] md:h-[32rem]"
      />
      <div>
        <p class="statement">Four fingers, a thumb, and everything that drives them.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">Each finger is its own module with its own motor. The modules sit side by side in the palm, the thumb slides on beside them, and the electronics sit under one curved shell that is the back of the hand.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-rule">The grey parts are the screws and nuts. The motors and the boards are inside, out of sight.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary mt-6" href={KIT_REQUEST}>Request a kit</a>
        <p class="meta mt-3 max-w-[40ch]">Kits are not for sale yet. Write to the four of us and tell us about your class.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <SectionLabel>One finger</SectionLabel>
    <div class="mt-8 grid items-start gap-x-12 gap-y-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.25fr)]">
      <div class="lg:order-2">
        <ModelViewer
          src="/models/finger-final-v3.glb"
          alt="3D model of one finger module: a three-segment finger on a long motor housing"
          label="One finger module"
          height="h-80 md:h-[26rem]"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="statement">One motor curls three segments.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">The motor turns a threaded rod. A block rides along the rod and pulls a link, and the links carry that one motion through all three segments of the finger, from straight to a 72° curl.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">It is the unit of the whole curriculum: small enough to understand completely, real enough to be worth programming.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary mt-6" href={p('/lessons/beginner/01-finger-module/')}>Open Lesson 1</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="parts">
    <SectionLabel>The parts</SectionLabel>
    <p class="statement mt-6">Every part of one hand is either printed or bought.</p>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-x-14 gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg">Printed</h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 border-t border-navy">
          {printed.map((b) => (
            <li class="border-b border-edge py-3.5">
              <p class="font-semibold">{b.item}</p>
              <p class="mt-0.5 text-rule">{b.note}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg">Bought</h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 border-t border-navy">
          {bought.map((b) => (
            <li class="border-b border-edge py-3.5">
              <p class="font-semibold">{b.item}{b.qty > 1 && <span class="ml-2 font-normal tabular-nums text-rule">×{b.qty}</span>}</p>
              <p class="mt-0.5 text-rule">{b.note}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="need">
    <SectionLabel>What you need</SectionLabel>
    <div class="mt-8 grid items-start gap-x-12 gap-y-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.5fr)]">
      <p class="statement">Besides the parts: a 3D printer, a computer, and hex keys.</p>
      <ul class="border-t border-navy">
        {needs.map((n) => (
          <li class="grid gap-x-8 gap-y-1 border-b border-edge py-3.5 md:grid-cols-[11rem_1fr]">
            <p class="font-semibold">{n.item}</p>
            <p class="text-rule">{n.note}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="cost">
    <SectionLabel>What it costs</SectionLabel>
    <div class="mt-8 grid items-start gap-x-12 gap-y-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.5fr)]">
      <div>
        <p class="statement">{money(bill.total)} in parts for one hand.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">That is every part the team has priced, the plastic for the printed parts, and a fifth on top for what is not listed yet. One hand is meant to be shared by a group of four students, so a class of {CLASS_SIZE} needs {classHands} hands: <strong>{money(bill.total * classHands)}</strong>.</p>
        <p class="mt-4"><a class="link" href={p('/problem/#compare')}>See it beside five other kits</a></p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-rule">This is the cost of the parts of the current prototype, not a selling price. Screws, wiring and the two push buttons are not priced one by one: they fall under the contingency.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="result-table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col" class="text-right!">How many</th><th scope="col" class="text-right!">Each</th><th scope="col" class="text-right!">Cost</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {cost.rows.map((r) => (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">{r.item}</th>
                  <td class="text-right!">{r.qty}</td>
                  <td class="text-right!">{money(r.unit)}</td>
                  <td class="text-right!">{money(r.qty * r.unit)}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Contingency ({cost.contingency * 100}%)</th>
                <td></td><td></td>
                <td class="text-right!">{money(bill.extra)}</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" class="font-bold!">Total</th>
                <td class="result"></td><td class="result"></td>
                <td class="result text-right! font-bold">{money(bill.total)}</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="meta mt-3">The team's cost table of {cost.date}. Unit prices are from the <a class="link" href={cost.src.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{cost.src.label}</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <SectionLabel>How a lesson works</SectionLabel>
    <p class="statement mt-6">Design it, build it, code it.</p>
    <p class="lede mt-3">Every lesson has three parts. Each part is one class session.</p>
    <ProcessRail steps={portionSteps} class="mt-10" />
    <a class="btn btn-secondary mt-10" href={p('/lessons/beginner/')}>Browse the lessons</a>
  </section>

  {/* The circuit is the one on the team's final prototype poster (24 Nov 2026), redrawn in
      CircuitDiagram.astro. The two-motor "Testing so far" table that stood above this section
      came from the earlier poster; the final poster has no testing table, so it is gone. */}
  <section class="section" id="circuit">
    <SectionLabel>Circuit</SectionLabel>
    <div class="mt-6 grid items-start gap-x-12 gap-y-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <p class="statement">Six motors on one Arduino.</p>
      <p>One Arduino Mega 2560 controls two motor shields, and each shield drives three DC motors. A tilt sensor shares the same connection, and two push buttons give control by hand. The motors run from their own 7.2 V battery. A Wi-Fi module is proposed and not built yet.</p>
    </div>
    <CircuitDiagram class="mt-8" />
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <SectionLabel>Specifications</SectionLabel>
    <div class="mt-8 grid items-start gap-x-12 gap-y-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.5fr)]">
      <div>
        <p class="statement">Printed parts, an Arduino, and ordinary screws.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">When a part breaks, print another. When a student wants a different finger, design one.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="result-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Spec</th><th scope="col">Value</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {specs.map((s) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" class="whitespace-nowrap">{s.k}</th>
                <td>{s.v}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
